From 093a39553d646815a13d72df74bfa5531212c360 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:55:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Make Teammates chat aware of all four products, not just
 two
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The chat's system prompt only described Showtime and Reputation
Manager, and had zero visibility into Cold Open or Whop Agent (which
alone has 15 skills, including the actual per-client "Connect Whop
Account" flow that pastes and health-checks a Whop Bot API key). A
user asking whether their Whop account was connected was hitting a
model with no idea that connection even existed as a real, checkable
thing in this app, only a vague "Whop isn't a platform I can check."

- Teach the workspace fetch to check all 4 products (isPackageInstalledInWorkspace
  for cold-open/whop-agent too, not just reputation-manager) and tag
  each client in the prompt with Cold Open enrollment / Whop Agent
  connection state, the same way Reputation Manager enrollment was
  already tagged.
- Add getWhopConnectionStatus (chat-status-queries.ts) — a real,
  workspace-scoped read of whop_agent_connections (credential type,
  circuit breaker state, disconnected-at, scope probe results), and a
  new read-only check_whop_connection tool that uses it.
- Rewrite the system prompt to name all four products up front, state
  plainly which are installed in this workspace, and disambiguate "is
  my Whop account connected" between the always-true dashboard login
  and the real, per-client Whop Agent connection state — resolving one
  of the two rather than assuming.
- Cold Open and Whop Agent's other 14 skills still have no chat tools
  (same honesty pattern already used for Reputation Manager's watch
  skills): the prompt now says so explicitly instead of the model
  having no idea those products exist at all.

