From b652238cfb3b1adefc7ce0becf33ab285d9cf657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:20:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Wire Cold Open and Whop Agent's real actions into
 Teammates chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes most of the remaining chat/dashboard capability gap: chat had a
product-install flag and a connection health check for Whop Agent, and
nothing at all for Cold Open, while the dashboard could actually run
14 more Whop Agent actions and toggle Cold Open's skills. Every
wrapper here calls the exact same service function its dashboard route
already calls (src/app/api/engagements/[id]/whop-agent/*,
.../skills/cold-open/[skillId]) — never a second execution path — and
inherits that route's existing safety gates for free rather than
reimplementing them:

- run_product_launch_preflight / run_bulk_promo_codes: dry-run-first
  per engagement (Section 8.2, isDryRunRequired) is enforced inside the
  service itself, not by chat.
- configure_cancel_discount / submit_dispute_evidence /
  flip_whop_ad_active: always queue a pendingAction (Section 8.3) a
  human approves in the dashboard's Approvals — nothing here ever
  writes live to Whop directly.
- draft_whop_ad creates a draft only (no spend); assemble_* tools are
  read-only.
- whop-connect (the raw Bot API key paste) is deliberately excluded,
  same hard rule as booking/email credentials — no raw secret ever
  goes through chat.
- Whop Agent's Drift Monitor, Refund/Dispute Velocity, and Daily
  Change Digest have no manual trigger anywhere in the app (cron/
  notification-only) — the prompt says so rather than fabricating one.
- enable_cold_open_skill mirrors the dashboard's own toggle route
  exactly, including both of its gates (icp-lock can't be turned on
  this way; every other skill needs icp-lock's onboarding to have run
  first). Cold Open's 6 other skills still only run on their own
  cadence once enabled — there's no "run now" for them anywhere, so
  none was invented here either.

New: src/lib/chat-whop-agent.ts (12 wrappers), src/lib/chat-cold-open.ts
(1 wrapper). route.ts gets the matching tool defs, dispatch branches,
and system-prompt rules, including a correction to
run_product_launch_preflight's own description: Section 8.2's dry-run
message tells the operator to "re-run with dryRun:false," but
runProductLaunchBatch (the function both chat and the dashboard's own
route call) never accepts a dryRun override — that bypass doesn't
actually exist anywhere in the app today for a single launch below the
4-product bulk-confirm threshold. The tool is honest about that rather
than fabricating a working bypass chat alone would have.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRxyo1ZXhb7Jft7LdiA4Ve
